1
00:00:01,203 --> 00:00:04,172
(Happiness for Sale)

2
00:00:04,173 --> 00:00:05,443
Nice to see you all.

3
00:00:06,343 --> 00:00:08,142
It's been a while, Jae Hyeon.

4
00:00:08,143 --> 00:00:10,552
- It's been so long. - You've gotten more muscular now.

5
00:00:10,553 --> 00:00:12,523
I'm getting in more shape now.

6
00:00:13,583 --> 00:00:15,382
- People say it's a new side of you. - Really?

7
00:00:15,383 --> 00:00:16,492
Everyone has been talking about you.

8
00:00:16,493 --> 00:00:18,253
- At Jang Woo's wedding, - Yes.

9
00:00:18,423 --> 00:00:20,462
Everyone kept looking at Jae Hyeon.

10
00:00:20,463 --> 00:00:22,169
- Right. He's so handsome. - Everyone took pictures of you.

11
00:00:22,193 --> 00:00:23,262
- This is his prime. - I was so surprised.

12
00:00:23,263 --> 00:00:24,532
I'm good at weddings, you know?

13
00:00:24,533 --> 00:00:25,663
Exactly.

14
00:00:26,663 --> 00:00:27,802
Just like your broad shoulders,

15
00:00:27,803 --> 00:00:29,172
- you're brimming with confidence. - Of course.

16
00:00:29,173 --> 00:00:31,772
- When it comes to weddings, - He got the poisonous needle later.

17
00:00:31,773 --> 00:00:32,903
I'm the best man.

18
00:00:33,773 --> 00:00:37,512
For today's clip, Kian84, CODE KUNST, and I worked together.

19
00:00:37,513 --> 00:00:38,673
We finished...

20
00:00:39,683 --> 00:00:40,742
a meaningful project.

21
00:00:40,743 --> 00:00:43,252
The three of you got together while I was away in Kazakhstan.

22
00:00:43,253 --> 00:00:44,613
We've been waiting for our chance.

23
00:00:44,883 --> 00:00:46,023
Gosh, you're so annoying.

24
00:00:46,253 --> 00:00:48,152
- What? - I'm done. I can't do this anymore.

25
00:00:48,153 --> 00:00:49,352
- What? - I've been waiting for that day.

26
00:00:49,353 --> 00:00:51,353
I wanted to join you for the flea market.

27
00:00:51,653 --> 00:00:53,622
- The flea market? - You're sulking...

28
00:00:53,623 --> 00:00:55,122
- just like Kkotbun. - I'm so sulking right now.

29
00:00:55,123 --> 00:00:56,683
He has the same personality as Kkotbun.

30
00:00:57,433 --> 00:00:58,532
You'll get over it quickly.

31
00:00:58,533 --> 00:00:59,933
- Right away. - Right away.

32
00:01:00,263 --> 00:01:01,863
How many years has it been?

33
00:01:02,163 --> 00:01:04,002
- I might see ghosts here. - It's the break of dawn.

34
00:01:04,003 --> 00:01:05,573
(Grand Opening, current time: 7am)

35
00:01:05,903 --> 00:01:08,543
This is scary. I might see ghosts here.

36
00:01:09,173 --> 00:01:10,713
I haven't been here in ages.

37
00:01:11,343 --> 00:01:12,483
Where did you go?

38
00:01:14,843 --> 00:01:18,513
(He carefully opens the door.)

39
00:01:20,223 --> 00:01:23,292
(An unfamiliar place)

40
00:01:23,293 --> 00:01:25,023
It's like I'm watching a movie.

41
00:01:27,263 --> 00:01:29,303
Gosh, the last time I was here was three years ago.

42
00:01:29,833 --> 00:01:31,192
- My gosh, seriously. - How mysterious.

43
00:01:31,193 --> 00:01:32,193
This looks strange.

44
00:01:32,763 --> 00:01:35,123
It looks like Hannibal Lecter might be in one of the cages.

45
00:01:36,003 --> 00:01:37,373
No one's living here, right?

46
00:01:39,003 --> 00:01:41,143
(He nervously walks in.)

47
00:01:41,743 --> 00:01:43,413
- It looks like a horror movie. - Right.

48
00:01:43,943 --> 00:01:45,912
- Or he's here to see a prisoner. - He's crying.

49
00:01:45,913 --> 00:01:47,713
- He's crying. He saw someone. - What is it?

50
00:01:49,853 --> 00:01:51,813
(Weeping)

51
00:01:52,053 --> 00:01:53,483
- Gosh, the piano. - What?

52
00:01:53,683 --> 00:01:54,683
What?

53
00:01:54,684 --> 00:01:56,323
- A piano? - I had the piano.

54
00:01:57,053 --> 00:01:58,393
Gosh, this is driving me crazy.

55
00:01:59,053 --> 00:02:01,092
I didn't even lock this. Come on.

56
00:02:01,093 --> 00:02:03,413
(He finally comes face to face with the mysterious space.)

57
00:02:04,063 --> 00:02:05,132
The piano...

58
00:02:05,133 --> 00:02:06,202
- It's your storage. - Yes.

59
00:02:06,203 --> 00:02:07,262
You have a separate storage space?

60
00:02:07,263 --> 00:02:08,362
- I do. - I see.

61
00:02:08,363 --> 00:02:10,732
It was my first time visiting it after moving.

62
00:02:10,733 --> 00:02:12,653
- You rarely use that. - I rarely go down there.

63
00:02:14,773 --> 00:02:16,612
Well, I'm sure you know...

64
00:02:16,613 --> 00:02:18,972
when I'm hooked on something, I buy first and regret later.

65
00:02:18,973 --> 00:02:20,843
In the end, I'm helping our economy.

66
00:02:21,213 --> 00:02:23,182
I help economy in many different fields.

67
00:02:23,183 --> 00:02:25,263
When I went down to my storage today, I was shocked.

68
00:02:25,613 --> 00:02:27,352
The music industry, restaurant industry,

69
00:02:27,353 --> 00:02:28,423
and publishing industry.

70
00:02:28,523 --> 00:02:30,603
I've been spending money in all of these industries.

71
00:02:31,323 --> 00:02:33,093
The piano. Darn.

72
00:02:33,693 --> 00:02:35,393
I didn't know I had the festive table.

73
00:02:36,393 --> 00:02:39,632
(It's full of items he hasn't seen in a while.)

74
00:02:39,633 --> 00:02:42,833
My gosh. This is completely new.

75
00:02:43,603 --> 00:02:45,372
(He used the piano to practice for the fan-meet 7 or 8 years ago.)

76
00:02:45,373 --> 00:02:46,843
My gosh. That was seven years ago.

77
00:02:47,843 --> 00:02:49,572
- It looks like a good piano. - It's a great piano.

78
00:02:49,573 --> 00:02:50,712
- Really? - Buying it was a big decision.

79
00:02:50,713 --> 00:02:52,313
(But he's been neglecting it for years.)

80
00:02:54,043 --> 00:02:55,713
Oh, the horse riding machine.

81
00:02:55,983 --> 00:02:57,012
- An equestrian simulator? - An equestrian simulator.

82
00:02:57,013 --> 00:02:58,283
I see. It's a workout machine.

83
00:02:59,623 --> 00:03:01,183
That was my first house in Geumho-dong.

84
00:03:01,623 --> 00:03:03,052
- That's... - I bought it after watching it...

85
00:03:03,053 --> 00:03:04,492
on a home-shopping channel.

86
00:03:04,493 --> 00:03:06,122
(He failed to get rid of it...)

87
00:03:06,123 --> 00:03:09,123
(when he opened Moomoo Store last time.)

88
00:03:10,293 --> 00:03:11,693
The machine was rotting in here.

89
00:03:11,833 --> 00:03:13,393
I wonder if anyone's going to buy this.

90
00:03:13,863 --> 00:03:16,973
To celebrate the new year, 2026,

91
00:03:17,333 --> 00:03:18,533
I'm starting a grand project.

92
00:03:18,833 --> 00:03:21,943
I'm going to hold the Grand Rainbow Bazaar.

93
00:03:22,503 --> 00:03:23,972
As for the hosts of the Grand Rainbow Bazaar,

94
00:03:23,973 --> 00:03:25,443
there's me.

95
00:03:25,943 --> 00:03:27,242
CODE KUNST is my co-host...

96
00:03:27,243 --> 00:03:29,553
whose wardrobe is ten times bigger than mine.

97
00:03:30,053 --> 00:03:32,293
Kian84 is also my co-host who has a lot of random items.

98
00:03:32,583 --> 00:03:35,053
The three of us will open the Grand Rainbow Bazaar.

99
00:03:36,253 --> 00:03:37,922
(Trend Sensitive Man)

100
00:03:37,923 --> 00:03:38,992
- Young 50s. - TSM.

101
00:03:38,993 --> 00:03:40,193
(Trend Sensitive Man)

102
00:03:40,793 --> 00:03:43,463
(TSM spends 1,000 dollars on his hobby.)

103
00:03:44,263 --> 00:03:46,302
- Do you still have that? - I do.

104
00:03:46,303 --> 00:03:48,663
(All the latest trends belong to me.)

105
00:03:49,503 --> 00:03:52,403
(He has all kinds of equipment, more than he can handle.)

106
00:03:53,343 --> 00:03:54,902
(Hyun Moo, the General Store Owner as he has countless hobbies)

107
00:03:54,903 --> 00:03:56,303
- You have so many hobbies. - Gosh.

108
00:03:57,513 --> 00:03:59,813
(Fashion represents me.)

109
00:04:00,613 --> 00:04:02,042
- He has so many clothes. - He must sell everything.

110
00:04:02,043 --> 00:04:03,053
He doesn't wear them all.

111
00:04:04,313 --> 00:04:06,582
(He has so many clothes that the rack is bending.)

112
00:04:06,583 --> 00:04:08,423
Once you put it away, you never wear it again.

113
00:04:09,023 --> 00:04:10,252
He has so much stuff.

114
00:04:10,253 --> 00:04:12,022
(I'll store my precious shoes in my room.)

115
00:04:12,023 --> 00:04:13,223
He has a lot of stuff too.

116
00:04:13,423 --> 00:04:14,892
- He has a lot of stuff. - I do.

117
00:04:14,893 --> 00:04:16,632
- Kian84 has a lot of stuff? - He has a lot of shoes.

118
00:04:16,633 --> 00:04:17,693
I have a lot of shoes.

119
00:04:18,993 --> 00:04:20,063
And random items.

120
00:04:21,563 --> 00:04:23,172
(The experts from Moomoo Store...)

121
00:04:23,173 --> 00:04:24,573
(and Seorae Outlet...)

122
00:04:25,473 --> 00:04:27,403
(have joined the bazaar.)

123
00:04:28,703 --> 00:04:31,243
(The grand hosts of the bazaar from different fields)

124
00:04:31,513 --> 00:04:34,883
All of our proceeds from the bazaar will go to a good cause.

125
00:04:35,013 --> 00:04:37,753
The three of us invited our friends...

126
00:04:38,013 --> 00:04:40,183
who wanted to be part of...

127
00:04:40,423 --> 00:04:41,923
helping out a good cause.

128
00:04:43,123 --> 00:04:46,592
(The Grand Rainbow Bazaar lives up to its name...)

129
00:04:46,593 --> 00:04:48,263
- I'm curious. - A lot of people came.

130
00:04:49,293 --> 00:04:50,662
I see. So many people turned up.

131
00:04:50,663 --> 00:04:52,363
(with its grand customers.)

132
00:04:52,933 --> 00:04:54,403
I don't know where to start.

133
00:04:55,063 --> 00:04:57,133
(Grabbing)

134
00:04:57,603 --> 00:04:58,773
Oh, my!

135
00:05:00,103 --> 00:05:02,442
What is it? Is it one of your early paintings?

136
00:05:02,443 --> 00:05:03,443
(Oh, my. This is...)

137
00:05:03,713 --> 00:05:04,813
I'm sorry, Kian84.

138
00:05:04,943 --> 00:05:06,642
- Why? I see. It's Kian84's. - What?

139
00:05:06,643 --> 00:05:07,882
- Is it Kian84's painting? - This is...

140
00:05:07,883 --> 00:05:09,042
I've been looking for it.

141
00:05:09,043 --> 00:05:10,183
I'm sorry, Kian84.

142
00:05:12,353 --> 00:05:15,083
- Oh, that? It was a long time ago. - It was a long time ago, right?

143
00:05:15,483 --> 00:05:16,893
- Wait. - Did he paint it?

144
00:05:17,093 --> 00:05:19,122
- It was about 10 years ago. - It was 10 years ago.

145
00:05:19,123 --> 00:05:23,032
(Kian84 gave a painting to Hyun Moo as a gift 10 years ago.)

146
00:05:23,033 --> 00:05:25,153
It's fine as long as one of us can ward off bad luck.

147
00:05:25,333 --> 00:05:27,403
I drew him a tiger for good luck.

148
00:05:28,003 --> 00:05:29,532
- Things worked out thanks to that. - I found it.

149
00:05:29,533 --> 00:05:30,602
Right. I put it back up.

150
00:05:30,603 --> 00:05:31,673
(Thank you.)

151
00:05:32,173 --> 00:05:34,943
This was when we first met. What a historical painting.

152
00:05:35,973 --> 00:05:37,773
It's the one I took with my parents.

153
00:05:38,073 --> 00:05:39,633
I should bring it to my parents' house.

154
00:05:41,213 --> 00:05:42,413
What's this doing here?

155
00:05:43,513 --> 00:05:45,913
Why did you put that in the storage? It's a family picture.

156
00:05:46,453 --> 00:05:48,093
I'm showing how to be the worst son ever.

157
00:05:48,323 --> 00:05:49,792
I see. That was the first step he took...

158
00:05:49,793 --> 00:05:51,252
- as a bad son. - Think of it...

159
00:05:51,253 --> 00:05:52,522
as my first step.

160
00:05:52,523 --> 00:05:54,899
(The pile of dust marks the start of his journey as a bad son.)

161
00:05:54,923 --> 00:05:56,032
(He takes out the inflator first.)

162
00:05:56,033 --> 00:05:57,393
I have another one at home.

163
00:05:57,993 --> 00:05:59,753
- Let's pull it out. - Why do you have that?

164
00:06:00,063 --> 00:06:01,133
Why do you have that?

165
00:06:01,633 --> 00:06:03,103
Why do I have so many inflators?

166
00:06:03,473 --> 00:06:04,732
I had five.

167
00:06:04,733 --> 00:06:06,173
(The next item is another inflator.)

168
00:06:06,603 --> 00:06:08,002
(It's full of items he bought on a whim...)

169
00:06:08,003 --> 00:06:09,443
(when he shouldn't have.)

170
00:06:09,713 --> 00:06:11,072
Why do I have an inflatable tub?

171
00:06:11,073 --> 00:06:12,783
You have an inflatable tub too?

172
00:06:14,943 --> 00:06:16,183
This is part of my history too.

173
00:06:18,213 --> 00:06:19,313
Okay.

174
00:06:20,883 --> 00:06:24,523
(He goes back home with his long history.)

175
00:06:26,593 --> 00:06:28,963
(Lugging)

176
00:06:29,863 --> 00:06:31,162
He has so much stuff.

177
00:06:31,163 --> 00:06:32,833
He recently bought the electric bicycle.

178
00:06:33,263 --> 00:06:34,363
I customized it.

179
00:06:38,303 --> 00:06:39,863
I pulled everything out the day before.

180
00:06:40,043 --> 00:06:41,602
That's a lot of work too.

181
00:06:41,603 --> 00:06:43,142
That's the most difficult part.

182
00:06:43,143 --> 00:06:44,373
There's so much stuff.

183
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:47,013
(It will take forever to organize them.)

184
00:06:48,343 --> 00:06:50,983
This is a great device. The ultrasonic eyeglass cleaner.

185
00:06:51,513 --> 00:06:54,083
(He begins organizing them one at a time with determination.)

186
00:06:54,823 --> 00:06:56,522
The sphincter strengthening device.

187
00:06:56,523 --> 00:06:57,692
A sphincter strengthening device?

188
00:06:57,693 --> 00:06:59,053
(He can't believe his ears.)

189
00:06:59,353 --> 00:07:01,063
Let me see what's in my atelier.

190
00:07:01,993 --> 00:07:04,133
(Is there anything else I can sell from this room?)

191
00:07:04,833 --> 00:07:06,562
All the rooms except the living room...

192
00:07:06,563 --> 00:07:08,263
- are used as storage. - Right.

193
00:07:08,933 --> 00:07:11,473
I should pull out the oven.

194
00:07:12,333 --> 00:07:15,803
Did I use this 2 or 3 times?

195
00:07:16,443 --> 00:07:19,143
I used it when I made schweinshaxe.

196
00:07:20,743 --> 00:07:21,912
A magic trick.

197
00:07:21,913 --> 00:07:23,082
(When did I learn the magic trick?)

198
00:07:23,083 --> 00:07:24,113
Let's sell it.

199
00:07:24,413 --> 00:07:25,813
It's from Yamaha.

200
00:07:26,183 --> 00:07:27,383
Wait. You have another one.

201
00:07:27,883 --> 00:07:30,122
I forgot that I had one in there and bought it again.

202
00:07:30,123 --> 00:07:32,293
- What? - So I have two pianos.

203
00:07:33,223 --> 00:07:35,023
This was only used to trick Danny. That's it.

204
00:07:36,193 --> 00:07:37,762
(The second piano was neglected after making him look good.)

205
00:07:37,763 --> 00:07:39,443
I didn't use it at all after that episode.

206
00:07:41,803 --> 00:07:43,273
What a waste.

207
00:07:44,633 --> 00:07:46,302
The thigh strengthening device.

208
00:07:46,303 --> 00:07:48,142
- How many times did you use it? - Three times?

209
00:07:48,143 --> 00:07:49,143
(He finds the forgotten thigh strengthening device.)

210
00:07:49,144 --> 00:07:51,243
- Everything is practically new. - They're all new.

211
00:07:52,573 --> 00:07:54,542
- A final check. - Gosh, look at his clothes.

212
00:07:54,543 --> 00:07:56,152
- You have so many clothes. - I tried to get rid of some.

213
00:07:56,153 --> 00:07:57,713
But I still have a lot left.

214
00:07:58,583 --> 00:08:00,782
(What's this?)

215
00:08:00,783 --> 00:08:02,323
Oh, it's a ukulele.

216
00:08:02,783 --> 00:08:03,993
This is...

217
00:08:04,393 --> 00:08:05,653
I only played it twice.

218
00:08:05,953 --> 00:08:06,993
It's brand-new.

219
00:08:07,623 --> 00:08:10,032
I have 2 pianos and 1 ukulele.

220
00:08:10,033 --> 00:08:11,163
I'm like a music major.

221
00:08:16,903 --> 00:08:18,003
Oh, no.

222
00:08:18,833 --> 00:08:20,703
(Struggling)

223
00:08:21,943 --> 00:08:23,013
For fire gazing.

224
00:08:25,343 --> 00:08:28,083
(Rattling)

225
00:08:28,683 --> 00:08:30,783
I didn't touch it after the fire gazing episode.

226
00:08:30,853 --> 00:08:31,983
The monitor?

227
00:08:32,983 --> 00:08:36,853
(He made good use of it when he went camping alone.)

228
00:08:37,753 --> 00:08:38,753
(A portable TV he used for fire gazing)

229
00:08:38,754 --> 00:08:39,994
I didn't use it after that day.

230
00:08:41,863 --> 00:08:42,933
Should I put this up?

231
00:08:45,793 --> 00:08:48,002
Gosh, it's such a good device. Why didn't I use it?

232
00:08:48,003 --> 00:08:50,273
- Oh, no. - I'm practically half crazy.

233
00:08:51,733 --> 00:08:54,773
(He takes pictures of it to post it on the app.)

234
00:08:56,643 --> 00:08:59,073
(Full of passion)

235
00:09:00,243 --> 00:09:01,383
Let's put it up.

236
00:09:03,713 --> 00:09:05,083
Gosh, I'm tired.

237
00:09:05,883 --> 00:09:08,953
(As he had an early morning, his entire body is aching.)

238
00:09:09,993 --> 00:09:12,393
(I should still try to sell it.)

239
00:09:12,993 --> 00:09:16,993
Buying and selling items on this app is trending nowadays.

240
00:09:17,863 --> 00:09:21,263
My gosh. This app has all the brands and items I love.

241
00:09:22,333 --> 00:09:25,003
(He selects the photos he took with love.)

242
00:09:25,503 --> 00:09:26,843
"Barely been used."

243
00:09:27,543 --> 00:09:29,143
"Four hundred dollars."

244
00:09:29,713 --> 00:09:30,742
Done.

245
00:09:30,743 --> 00:09:32,773
(I hope I can sell it fast.)

246
00:09:33,383 --> 00:09:34,743
It looks like I'm moving.

247
00:09:36,383 --> 00:09:37,383
Okay.

248
00:09:37,384 --> 00:09:40,583
(He's taking the items for the bazaar out of his house?)

249
00:09:41,283 --> 00:09:43,193
All right. Let's go.

250
00:09:45,823 --> 00:09:48,693
(Loading)

251
00:09:49,733 --> 00:09:50,862
(He loads the car with the items 1 by 1.)

252
00:09:50,863 --> 00:09:52,393
My goodness.

253
00:09:52,963 --> 00:09:53,963
I have no more space left.

254
00:09:53,964 --> 00:09:55,404
You can't fit everything in the car.

255
00:09:56,003 --> 00:09:57,003
My gosh.

256
00:09:57,004 --> 00:09:59,524
(Just like that, he leaves his house and heads somewhere else.)

257
00:10:00,173 --> 00:10:01,813
Seriously. I really hope I can sell them.

258
00:10:02,673 --> 00:10:04,313
My house is too small to hold the bazaar.

259
00:10:04,643 --> 00:10:05,942
So I needed a bigger space.

260
00:10:05,943 --> 00:10:09,753
I thought of a place that could give us the concept store vibe.

261
00:10:10,183 --> 00:10:11,453
I had everything in my head.

262
00:10:12,583 --> 00:10:14,822
(Kian84 and CODE KUNST are waiting for him at the place.)

263
00:10:14,823 --> 00:10:16,792
- Let's hang all the jackets here. - Yes.

264
00:10:16,793 --> 00:10:18,353
- I see. - That's Kian84's studio.

265
00:10:19,763 --> 00:10:21,363
It's hard to find a big space like that.

266
00:10:21,923 --> 00:10:23,832
My music studio is smaller than this.

267
00:10:23,833 --> 00:10:25,262
It's a nice place.

268
00:10:25,263 --> 00:10:26,363
The location is good too.

269
00:10:28,333 --> 00:10:30,333
Where's Ae Ong? I don't see your cat.

270
00:10:30,603 --> 00:10:32,733
I checked, and Ae Ong was in the usual spot.

271
00:10:34,443 --> 00:10:35,802
(The two of them are displaying the clothes...)

272
00:10:35,803 --> 00:10:37,143
(before Hyun Moo arrives.)

273
00:10:38,313 --> 00:10:39,472
Gosh, you have a lot of clothes.

274
00:10:39,473 --> 00:10:40,812
(Neatly hanging on the rack)

275
00:10:40,813 --> 00:10:42,313
(Looking sharp)

276
00:10:43,083 --> 00:10:45,453
(Meanwhile, Kian84...)

277
00:10:46,553 --> 00:10:49,183
(is hanging the clothes without much care.)

278
00:10:49,953 --> 00:10:52,293
(He finishes displaying them in an instant.)

279
00:10:52,693 --> 00:10:55,293
- Are you done with your clothes? - Yes, I'm done.

280
00:10:55,993 --> 00:10:57,563
(Observing)

281
00:10:58,133 --> 00:11:00,032
- Kian84. When you hang them, - Yes?

282
00:11:00,033 --> 00:11:01,303
They have to look nice.

283
00:11:01,803 --> 00:11:04,132
- How do you do that? - Make sure they're hanging neatly.

284
00:11:04,133 --> 00:11:05,332
If it's hanging like this,

285
00:11:05,333 --> 00:11:06,773
- Okay. - they won't want to buy it.

286
00:11:06,843 --> 00:11:08,163
- Really? I'm new to this. - Yes.

287
00:11:09,273 --> 00:11:11,572
- Make sure it's aligned? - When you hang it neatly,

288
00:11:11,573 --> 00:11:13,443
it looks stylish.

289
00:11:13,643 --> 00:11:14,682
Right.

290
00:11:14,683 --> 00:11:17,413
If it's asymmetrical, it looks like it's been stretched.

291
00:11:17,783 --> 00:11:20,223
- Then it looks worn. - Right. It'd look worn.

292
00:11:20,753 --> 00:11:22,323
You're right. Like this?

293
00:11:23,323 --> 00:11:24,993
- Yes. That's great. - Like this?

294
00:11:25,923 --> 00:11:28,092
A lot of people fall for this.

295
00:11:28,093 --> 00:11:30,063
- It's really important. - Right.

296
00:11:30,863 --> 00:11:33,233
(Neatly folding the pants)

297
00:11:35,303 --> 00:11:36,743
CODE KUNST looks professional today.

298
00:11:37,433 --> 00:11:39,573
The hangers should face the same side.

299
00:11:40,503 --> 00:11:41,902
Clothes look great...

300
00:11:41,903 --> 00:11:44,303
- when they're hung neatly. - Right. I should've been there.

301
00:11:44,573 --> 00:11:45,672
I should redo mine.

302
00:11:45,673 --> 00:11:46,682
(I want them to look nice too.)

303
00:11:46,683 --> 00:11:48,112
No. That's not necessary.

304
00:11:48,113 --> 00:11:49,213
I did an awful job.

305
00:11:50,413 --> 00:11:53,182
If there are too many clothes on the rack, people miss a few.

306
00:11:53,183 --> 00:11:55,063
I must make sure there's still some space left.

307
00:11:56,253 --> 00:11:57,322
- Like this. It should be... - Didn't you work...

308
00:11:57,323 --> 00:11:58,392
at a clothing shop?

309
00:11:58,393 --> 00:11:59,592
Yes. I worked at many clothing shops.

310
00:11:59,593 --> 00:12:01,062
Oh, right. I remember hearing you say...

311
00:12:01,063 --> 00:12:02,323
you worked at clothing shops.

312
00:12:02,693 --> 00:12:04,332
People will overlook some items if the rack is overfilled.

313
00:12:04,333 --> 00:12:05,933
(Skillful)

314
00:12:06,503 --> 00:12:08,533
It was around the time I was turning 24.

315
00:12:08,903 --> 00:12:12,373
Back then, I used to work at a clothing store during the day.

316
00:12:12,573 --> 00:12:14,342
I worked at department stores and vintage stores.

317
00:12:14,343 --> 00:12:15,583
I worked there for a long time.

318
00:12:16,003 --> 00:12:17,712
It's really important...

319
00:12:17,713 --> 00:12:21,883
to hang the clothes properly, so they don't look stretched out.

320
00:12:22,083 --> 00:12:23,452
The moment they don't look symmetrical on hangers,

321
00:12:23,453 --> 00:12:26,213
clothes look stretched and worn.

322
00:12:26,583 --> 00:12:28,983
I tried to hang them while making sure they looked balanced.

323
00:12:29,653 --> 00:12:30,922
When I was a high school senior,

324
00:12:30,923 --> 00:12:33,593
there was a certificate called Fashion Shop Master.

325
00:12:33,993 --> 00:12:35,523
I studied hard for the certificate.

326
00:12:36,293 --> 00:12:38,833
Try not to buy clothes displayed on the mannequins.

327
00:12:39,263 --> 00:12:40,932
The clothes on the mannequins?

328
00:12:40,933 --> 00:12:42,402
Here's why. On mannequins,

329
00:12:42,403 --> 00:12:44,203
- their belly button is here. - That's true.

330
00:12:44,433 --> 00:12:46,942
If you look closely, the mannequins are always standing on their toes.

331
00:12:46,943 --> 00:12:49,172
- Right. Pins are on their feet. - That's right.

332
00:12:49,173 --> 00:12:50,742
- They're standing on their toes. - They're wearing high heels.

333
00:12:50,743 --> 00:12:52,172
- Let's say you buy the same outfit. - Okay.

334
00:12:52,173 --> 00:12:54,842
- "How come it looks different?" - Right.

335
00:12:54,843 --> 00:12:57,053
- Hanging them neatly is crucial. - Right.

336
00:12:57,913 --> 00:13:00,633
You did this before. Do you have any useful tips on selling clothes?

337
00:13:00,923 --> 00:13:02,883
You can't lie to the customers.

338
00:13:03,053 --> 00:13:05,613
Let's say everyone can tell the clothes don't look good on them.

339
00:13:06,093 --> 00:13:07,762
- "Gosh, it looks great on you." - Right.

340
00:13:07,763 --> 00:13:08,922
- Right. - If you try to lie...

341
00:13:08,923 --> 00:13:10,932
When salespeople tell you they aren't for you,

342
00:13:10,933 --> 00:13:12,009
they instantly earn your trust.

343
00:13:12,033 --> 00:13:13,432
- Right. - They actually sound trustworthy.

344
00:13:13,433 --> 00:13:14,832
You have to work with the customers.

345
00:13:14,833 --> 00:13:16,339
For example, let's say they try on some clothes.

346
00:13:16,363 --> 00:13:18,002
Instead of saying, "That's not for you," you say,

347
00:13:18,003 --> 00:13:19,942
- "This looks better on you." - Right.

348
00:13:19,943 --> 00:13:21,243
- Then... - I see.

349
00:13:22,103 --> 00:13:24,349
If we crowd the rack more than this, we can't sell anything.

350
00:13:24,373 --> 00:13:25,413
This is perfect.

351
00:13:25,713 --> 00:13:29,113
If the rack is too crowded, nothing really stands out.

352
00:13:30,013 --> 00:13:31,452
Here's a tip.

353
00:13:31,453 --> 00:13:33,383
- To make them look fancy, - Okay.

354
00:13:33,883 --> 00:13:35,383
I have to misalign the racks.

355
00:13:35,883 --> 00:13:38,693
- I see. Like in a zigzag line? - Length should look different.

356
00:13:39,193 --> 00:13:40,222
That makes them look fancy.

357
00:13:40,223 --> 00:13:42,022
That way, they can see the clothes in the back when entering.

358
00:13:42,023 --> 00:13:43,363
For the three-dimensional feel?

359
00:13:44,263 --> 00:13:45,932
- You're right. It's much better. - Yes.

360
00:13:45,933 --> 00:13:46,933
It looks like we have more clothes.

361
00:13:46,934 --> 00:13:48,132
- You're right. - You had a strategy.

362
00:13:48,133 --> 00:13:50,232
- Of course. - You made good use of the space.

363
00:13:50,233 --> 00:13:52,703
My gosh, CODE KUNST. You're different.

364
00:13:53,603 --> 00:13:56,242
- Your clothes are more expensive. - Yes.

365
00:13:56,243 --> 00:13:57,942
- My clothes are cheap. - Yes.

366
00:13:57,943 --> 00:13:59,912
When they're thinking about buying your clothes,

367
00:13:59,913 --> 00:14:01,883
we can give away my clothes as freebies.

368
00:14:02,613 --> 00:14:04,882
The best piece of clothing I have is from Levi's.

369
00:14:04,883 --> 00:14:08,223
Let's run that scenario. "Gosh, this is so cute."

370
00:14:08,353 --> 00:14:09,852
"If you buy that, you get this for free."

371
00:14:09,853 --> 00:14:10,992
"They come as a set."

372
00:14:10,993 --> 00:14:12,299
- Yes. Right? - It looks like a better deal then.

373
00:14:12,323 --> 00:14:14,722
"Wear this when you go out. And wear this when you come home."

374
00:14:14,723 --> 00:14:16,832
- That's right. - That's a great strategy.

375
00:14:16,833 --> 00:14:18,793
I should put some of your clothes on my rack.

376
00:14:19,293 --> 00:14:21,562
Your clothes make my clothes look fancy.

377
00:14:21,563 --> 00:14:22,962
That's a great strategy.

378
00:14:22,963 --> 00:14:24,432
You guys mixed up the clothes.

379
00:14:24,433 --> 00:14:25,472
- Right? - We did.

380
00:14:25,473 --> 00:14:27,642
That's why I was so confused.

381
00:14:27,643 --> 00:14:29,672
- Think about it. - That was our strategy.

382
00:14:29,673 --> 00:14:30,812
- But... - I was worried that...

383
00:14:30,813 --> 00:14:31,972
if we separated our clothes, they'd only buy his.

384
00:14:31,973 --> 00:14:33,882
I thought, "These clothes look great."

385
00:14:33,883 --> 00:14:35,542
Then I went, "My gosh. What's this?" I was shocked.

386
00:14:35,543 --> 00:14:37,713
Come on. My clothes didn't look that bad.

387
00:14:38,013 --> 00:14:41,082
Actually, Kian84 had several pieces of clothing that looked great.

388
00:14:41,083 --> 00:14:42,282
- He did. - Yes.

389
00:14:42,283 --> 00:14:43,892
I only brought good clothes.

390
00:14:43,893 --> 00:14:45,023
- Of course. - Yes.

391
00:14:46,353 --> 00:14:48,093
(Placing good clothes on the rack)

392
00:14:49,523 --> 00:14:51,739
(Removing dust with a lint roller like a talented salesman)

393
00:14:51,763 --> 00:14:53,192
- Just as I expected. - I can see he's experienced.

394
00:14:53,193 --> 00:14:54,202
Right.

395
00:14:54,203 --> 00:14:55,803
(Setting up the clothes smoothly)

396
00:14:56,433 --> 00:14:57,702
Some of them were unopened?

397
00:14:57,703 --> 00:15:00,443
Gosh. Just how many clothes do you have at home?

398
00:15:00,573 --> 00:15:02,743
(Working hard)

399
00:15:03,443 --> 00:15:05,073
I also brought comic books.

400
00:15:06,243 --> 00:15:07,713
- Gosh, you have big feet. - Yes.

401
00:15:08,313 --> 00:15:09,642
(Displaying an expensive item on an elevated platform)

402
00:15:09,643 --> 00:15:11,213
- A laptop too? - A laptop? My gosh.

403
00:15:12,813 --> 00:15:14,583
(Checking)

404
00:15:14,783 --> 00:15:16,503
- Could you help me here, Sung Woo? - Okay.

405
00:15:16,793 --> 00:15:18,092
The TV? One, two, three.

406
00:15:18,093 --> 00:15:19,522
(I should sell the TV too.)

407
00:15:19,523 --> 00:15:22,922
Wait. Did you decide to sell it on the spot?

408
00:15:22,923 --> 00:15:23,962
All right.

409
00:15:23,963 --> 00:15:25,532
I kept thinking until we finished.

410
00:15:25,533 --> 00:15:27,102
"What else could I sell?"

411
00:15:27,103 --> 00:15:28,983
- Let's put it there for now. - It looks great.

412
00:15:30,473 --> 00:15:32,302
Concept stores these days have a comfy vibe like that.

413
00:15:32,303 --> 00:15:33,543
- Right. - We're done.

414
00:15:35,043 --> 00:15:36,483
You did a great job organizing them.

415
00:15:36,543 --> 00:15:38,112
- Don't they look neat? - Right.

416
00:15:38,113 --> 00:15:39,983
My gosh. Hey, this looks pretty legit.

417
00:15:40,683 --> 00:15:42,143
You guys have a lot of great items.

418
00:15:42,843 --> 00:15:43,852
(It turns into a concept store in no time.)

419
00:15:43,853 --> 00:15:45,483
They all look brand new.

420
00:15:46,653 --> 00:15:48,352
You guys have an amazing taste.

421
00:15:48,353 --> 00:15:51,292
He and I have known each other for a long time now.

422
00:15:51,293 --> 00:15:53,252
- Our teamwork was amazing. - Right.

423
00:15:53,253 --> 00:15:56,122
But the thing is, CODE KUNST told me...

424
00:15:56,123 --> 00:15:58,092
how we were going to arrange and place everything.

425
00:15:58,093 --> 00:15:59,562
He easily convinced me.

426
00:15:59,563 --> 00:16:01,802
Now that you guys finished setting up,

427
00:16:01,803 --> 00:16:03,062
it looks like a real concept store.

428
00:16:03,063 --> 00:16:05,133
- Right. - It's got everything.

429
00:16:05,803 --> 00:16:07,243
Do you want to go and buy some food?

430
00:16:07,843 --> 00:16:09,072
Let's buy some coffee too.

431
00:16:09,073 --> 00:16:10,142
Let's grab a cup of coffee.

432
00:16:10,143 --> 00:16:12,713
- Let's go down and buy coffee. - Yes.

433
00:16:12,773 --> 00:16:14,343
We did a great job and were fast too.

434
00:16:15,243 --> 00:16:16,513
- It looks great. - Yes.

435
00:16:17,213 --> 00:16:20,723
We need to think more carefully when we buy new things.

436
00:16:21,053 --> 00:16:24,352
No. I'm sure we had a good reason when we bought them.

437
00:16:24,353 --> 00:16:25,792
- We did, right? - Yes.

438
00:16:25,793 --> 00:16:27,823
- That's right. - Everything had a reason.

439
00:16:28,393 --> 00:16:30,313
- It felt great when I bought them. - Of course.

440
00:16:32,033 --> 00:16:33,232
- What? - He's here.

441
00:16:33,233 --> 00:16:34,433
Hyun Moo must be here.

442
00:16:35,963 --> 00:16:37,003
Like this?

443
00:16:37,903 --> 00:16:39,602
- You're here. - My gosh.

444
00:16:39,603 --> 00:16:40,942
We were leaving to buy some gimbap.

445
00:16:40,943 --> 00:16:43,072
Do you want to come with us to buy gimbap and coffee?

446
00:16:43,073 --> 00:16:44,173
I ought to.

447
00:16:45,613 --> 00:16:46,782
(He says yes without a moment of hesitation.)

448
00:16:46,783 --> 00:16:47,842
I was hungry that morning.

449
00:16:47,843 --> 00:16:49,412
You didn't think about it even for a second.

450
00:16:49,413 --> 00:16:51,613
- They were getting food. - As soon as you got there...

451
00:16:52,213 --> 00:16:53,312
- What's that? - I have so much stuff.

452
00:16:53,313 --> 00:16:54,822
- I'm going to sell everything. - Come in.

453
00:16:54,823 --> 00:16:55,982
Is that a pogo stick?

454
00:16:55,983 --> 00:16:57,292
- No. - Is this everything?

455
00:16:57,293 --> 00:16:58,492
No. I have...

456
00:16:58,493 --> 00:16:59,922
- about 50 times as much. - Give it to me.

457
00:16:59,923 --> 00:17:02,092
- Give that to me. - Let's move everything first then.

458
00:17:02,093 --> 00:17:04,133
- Let's organize them with coffee. - Let's do that.

459
00:17:04,263 --> 00:17:06,032
Could you help me? Should I unload them then?

460
00:17:06,033 --> 00:17:07,102
- Food... Yes. - Yes.

461
00:17:07,103 --> 00:17:08,802
We'll move them inside. You can just bring them...

462
00:17:08,803 --> 00:17:09,832
- to the door. - Okay.

463
00:17:09,833 --> 00:17:12,273
(The three of them will work together to organize the items.)

464
00:17:12,503 --> 00:17:14,772
We can hang more clothes here.

465
00:17:14,773 --> 00:17:15,843
Okay.

466
00:17:16,603 --> 00:17:18,912
They'd rather want to buy my fishing rod than that.

467
00:17:18,913 --> 00:17:20,682
(They'd rather want to buy my fishing rod than that.)

468
00:17:20,683 --> 00:17:22,682
The air pump has never been used.

469
00:17:22,683 --> 00:17:24,212
- I'd hate to buy that. - Seriously.

470
00:17:24,213 --> 00:17:26,093
(No one's warming up to the idea of buying it.)

471
00:17:27,053 --> 00:17:29,353
(His car is filled with strange items.)

472
00:17:30,623 --> 00:17:31,692
(Chuckling)

473
00:17:31,693 --> 00:17:33,963
- Who can pull this off? - What is it?

474
00:17:34,993 --> 00:17:36,122
Come on.

475
00:17:36,123 --> 00:17:37,593
What's that? Hold on.

476
00:17:37,633 --> 00:17:39,032
The pair is from Gucci.

477
00:17:39,033 --> 00:17:40,132
It's from a luxury brand.

478
00:17:40,133 --> 00:17:41,802
- The pair is from Gucci. - Really?

479
00:17:41,803 --> 00:17:43,602
I got a 70 percent discount on an overseas shopping site.

480
00:17:43,603 --> 00:17:44,702
So I had to buy them.

481
00:17:44,703 --> 00:17:45,733
The shoes...

482
00:17:47,143 --> 00:17:49,424
- I thought they were interest-free. - I had to buy them.

483
00:17:49,703 --> 00:17:52,112
- They're a beautiful pair, though. - They're a good pair.

484
00:17:52,113 --> 00:17:53,612
- They're a beautiful pair. - Yes. I like them.

485
00:17:53,613 --> 00:17:55,942
They're made of real leather and from Gucci.

486
00:17:55,943 --> 00:17:58,053
The pair didn't meet the right owner.

487
00:17:58,253 --> 00:18:00,182
I was once hooked on this overseas shopping site.

488
00:18:00,183 --> 00:18:01,982
- These promotions pop up. - Okay.

489
00:18:01,983 --> 00:18:03,722
- You know the brand, Balenciaga? - Yes.

490
00:18:03,723 --> 00:18:05,422
- Their windbreaker... - Right.

491
00:18:05,423 --> 00:18:07,992
- had a 90 percent discount. - The one in a neon color? Right?

492
00:18:07,993 --> 00:18:10,063
- The green windbreaker. - Yes.

493
00:18:10,233 --> 00:18:12,092
- The size was triple extra-large. - Okay.

494
00:18:12,093 --> 00:18:13,962
But there was only one left. So I bought it.

495
00:18:13,963 --> 00:18:15,033
Really?

496
00:18:15,763 --> 00:18:17,803
I wore it like a dress.

497
00:18:18,703 --> 00:18:20,542
It didn't fit me at all. The sleeves covered my hands.

498
00:18:20,543 --> 00:18:21,672
(That's how Moomoo's oversized look was made.)

499
00:18:21,673 --> 00:18:23,543
I bought the shoes when I bought the jacket.

500
00:18:24,113 --> 00:18:25,212
A neon-colored windbreaker...

501
00:18:25,213 --> 00:18:26,313
- and red shoes? - Yes.

502
00:18:26,473 --> 00:18:28,142
Hyun Moo, you're going to get arrested.

503
00:18:28,143 --> 00:18:30,253
(A wrong mix of items)

504
00:18:31,253 --> 00:18:33,213
- I brought everything. - Seriously.

505
00:18:33,583 --> 00:18:35,182
- Some random items. - You brought everything.

506
00:18:35,183 --> 00:18:36,382
Miscellaneous items.

507
00:18:36,383 --> 00:18:39,292
Our flea market was fun to browse thanks to your items.

508
00:18:39,293 --> 00:18:40,533
Right. I brought various items.

509
00:18:42,263 --> 00:18:43,462
(Heavy)

510
00:18:43,463 --> 00:18:45,893
What's this? He brought a lie detector toy.

511
00:18:46,363 --> 00:18:48,463
Why did you have that at your house?

512
00:18:51,303 --> 00:18:52,303
(The room is filled with mysterious items.)

513
00:18:52,304 --> 00:18:53,773
The room filled up fast.

514
00:18:54,973 --> 00:18:56,502
- Kian84. - Yes.

515
00:18:56,503 --> 00:18:57,743
What's your take on this?

516
00:18:59,413 --> 00:19:00,442
He brought pre-made croissant dough.

517
00:19:00,443 --> 00:19:01,559
- What do you think? - What?

518
00:19:01,583 --> 00:19:02,683
- What? - What's that?

519
00:19:03,213 --> 00:19:05,482
- You can bake croissants. - Why did he bring them?

520
00:19:05,483 --> 00:19:07,203
He must've taken them out from the freezer.

521
00:19:07,853 --> 00:19:10,223
- He was just cleaning his fridge. - That's...

522
00:19:11,223 --> 00:19:13,252
- They were in the freezer. - I wasn't going to sell them.

523
00:19:13,253 --> 00:19:14,492
I brought them for a reason.

524
00:19:14,493 --> 00:19:15,762
- I see. - Really?

525
00:19:15,763 --> 00:19:17,762
We didn't know his grand plan at that time.

526
00:19:17,763 --> 00:19:19,193
- Right. - Really?

527
00:19:21,303 --> 00:19:22,963
This looks pretty nice.

528
00:19:23,973 --> 00:19:25,602
Did you already set everything up?

529
00:19:25,603 --> 00:19:26,919
(The 2nd-floor concept store is neatly organized.)

530
00:19:26,943 --> 00:19:28,743
I see a few items I want to buy.

531
00:19:29,303 --> 00:19:30,573
I wanted to shop like crazy.

532
00:19:30,713 --> 00:19:32,313
(That's typical Hyun Moo.)

533
00:19:32,843 --> 00:19:35,183
- Hyun Moo. Customers are coming... - Yes.

534
00:19:35,543 --> 00:19:37,782
- at 10am. - Already?

535
00:19:37,783 --> 00:19:40,023
- We have an hour left. - We must organize them quickly.

536
00:19:40,353 --> 00:19:42,353
- I'll set this place up. - Okay.

537
00:19:43,593 --> 00:19:45,592
They're quite useful.

538
00:19:45,593 --> 00:19:46,822
(He takes out a box from a corner.)

539
00:19:46,823 --> 00:19:48,343
They can just grab whatever they need.

540
00:19:48,823 --> 00:19:50,939
- Just the cords, not the devices? - Everyone needs cords.

541
00:19:50,963 --> 00:19:52,093
Right.

542
00:19:52,833 --> 00:19:54,403
I see. They're freebies?

543
00:19:54,503 --> 00:19:55,662
- I see. - No.

544
00:19:55,663 --> 00:19:56,832
We must charge them at least a dollar.

545
00:19:56,833 --> 00:19:58,132
- For the cords? - For the cords.

546
00:19:58,133 --> 00:19:59,332
I have so many of them.

547
00:19:59,333 --> 00:20:00,942
- Right. - But doesn't everyone have...

548
00:20:00,943 --> 00:20:02,543
cords they don't use at home?

549
00:20:03,203 --> 00:20:04,743
I'm sure someone will need them.

550
00:20:09,083 --> 00:20:10,143
Hello.

551
00:20:12,483 --> 00:20:14,353
- You're here. - Already?

552
00:20:14,653 --> 00:20:15,783
Who's here?

553
00:20:16,323 --> 00:20:17,652
Yes. I'm in the parking lot.

554
00:20:17,653 --> 00:20:19,653
- Okay. I'll come down now. - Okay.

555
00:20:20,423 --> 00:20:21,992
- The truck is here. - You brought more stuff?

556
00:20:21,993 --> 00:20:23,062
- Yes. - What?

557
00:20:23,063 --> 00:20:24,192
I brought everything from my house.

558
00:20:24,193 --> 00:20:25,993
What did he bring? Oh, my.

559
00:20:27,033 --> 00:20:29,302
I wonder if we'll find the owner for the equestrian machine.

560
00:20:29,303 --> 00:20:31,432
- Gosh. That's... - There must be a separate storage.

561
00:20:31,433 --> 00:20:33,703
When I saw the truck, I didn't know what to do.

562
00:20:35,343 --> 00:20:37,172
- What's this? - That's...

563
00:20:37,173 --> 00:20:39,272
- What's that? - You can put trays in there.

564
00:20:39,273 --> 00:20:41,043
Then you can put the oven on top.

565
00:20:41,443 --> 00:20:42,783
You can bake bread with it.

566
00:20:43,013 --> 00:20:44,682
- Why did he buy that? - Even...

567
00:20:44,683 --> 00:20:47,252
- I thought it was for Pilates. - Same here.

568
00:20:47,253 --> 00:20:48,553
It's custom-made.

569
00:20:49,183 --> 00:20:52,922
Even cafes and bakeries don't have it. It's a high-end oven.

570
00:20:52,923 --> 00:20:54,762
- But you had it at home? - To bake bread?

571
00:20:54,763 --> 00:20:57,932
Pastry chefs were so envious. "How do you have this?"

572
00:20:57,933 --> 00:20:59,332
(The oven and rack are sought after by pastry chefs.)

573
00:20:59,333 --> 00:21:02,332
For the past ten years, I held flea markets...

574
00:21:02,333 --> 00:21:05,403
from time to time. But I've never seen them before.

575
00:21:05,773 --> 00:21:09,003
He brought a great variety of items.

576
00:21:09,943 --> 00:21:11,373
(Thinking)

577
00:21:11,473 --> 00:21:13,012
I respect him.

578
00:21:13,013 --> 00:21:16,213
We'll all leave this world empty-handed.

579
00:21:16,813 --> 00:21:19,813
So while he's alive, he wants to enjoy a lot of things.

580
00:21:20,283 --> 00:21:22,323
That's my understanding of him.

581
00:21:22,453 --> 00:21:24,093
In every interview, it sounds like...

582
00:21:24,493 --> 00:21:26,552
- He treats you like you're dead. - you want me dead.

583
00:21:26,553 --> 00:21:28,153
(The poor, materialistic soul is angry.)

584
00:21:28,893 --> 00:21:30,332
My gosh. That's dangerous.

585
00:21:30,333 --> 00:21:32,033
- No. - Gosh, what are you doing?

586
00:21:32,593 --> 00:21:34,833
- This? - Gosh. He's so manly.

587
00:21:35,733 --> 00:21:37,432
Kian84, are you going to be okay?

588
00:21:37,433 --> 00:21:39,603
- What? It's not heavy. - Are you okay?

589
00:21:40,403 --> 00:21:42,603
That's a heavy stone. But he's carrying that too.

590
00:21:43,503 --> 00:21:45,143
It's a millstone.

591
00:21:45,213 --> 00:21:46,943
- That's really heavy. - Yes.

592
00:21:47,143 --> 00:21:48,582
Whenever I see things like that, I want to carry them.

593
00:21:48,583 --> 00:21:50,283
He carried the rack with the millstone.

594
00:21:52,083 --> 00:21:53,853
Let's put this on the first floor.

595
00:21:55,383 --> 00:21:57,322
(Large items that are hard to see at flea markets)

596
00:21:57,323 --> 00:21:59,883
I thought I was going to break my back while carrying his stuff.

597
00:22:00,423 --> 00:22:02,463
The equestrian machine is really heavy too.

598
00:22:03,733 --> 00:22:05,833
It gives a great workout. I'm serious.

599
00:22:06,363 --> 00:22:07,702
- Hyun Moo. - Yes.

600
00:22:07,703 --> 00:22:11,033
Organize your things. We'll go and buy some food.

601
00:22:11,133 --> 00:22:13,572
- I want an inside-out gimbap. - What?

602
00:22:13,573 --> 00:22:15,102
- You're an oldie. - Gosh, no.

603
00:22:15,103 --> 00:22:17,112
- Are you still in the 90s? - Preferences don't change.

604
00:22:17,113 --> 00:22:19,713
- I was in elementary school then. - The one with the vegetables.

605
00:22:19,843 --> 00:22:21,742
- I don't like tuna gimbap. - We'll just get something for you.

606
00:22:21,743 --> 00:22:24,153
No. I want the inside-out gimbap with vegetables.

607
00:22:25,983 --> 00:22:28,123
(He goes up to the 2nd floor after sending them off.)

608
00:22:28,883 --> 00:22:30,793
(Grabbing)

609
00:22:31,553 --> 00:22:33,252
There's something fishy about Hyun Moo.

610
00:22:33,253 --> 00:22:34,892
(He goes down to the 1st floor with the croissant dough, )

611
00:22:34,893 --> 00:22:36,493
(looking somewhat suspicious.)

612
00:22:39,833 --> 00:22:41,432
(Pouring out)

613
00:22:41,433 --> 00:22:42,603
What is he doing?

614
00:22:43,363 --> 00:22:45,203
Hyun Moo keeps creating more work.

615
00:22:45,403 --> 00:22:46,633
He's suspicious.

616
00:22:48,243 --> 00:22:51,313
(He puts them straight in the oven.)

617
00:22:52,813 --> 00:22:54,912
(Is he running the oven?)

618
00:22:54,913 --> 00:22:56,143
The scent marketing.

619
00:22:56,813 --> 00:23:00,353
Why do you think bakeries open early in the morning?

620
00:23:00,923 --> 00:23:02,052
They spread the smell of bread on the streets...

621
00:23:02,053 --> 00:23:03,952
- and make people line up. - That's right.

622
00:23:03,953 --> 00:23:06,123
When people smell bread,

623
00:23:06,353 --> 00:23:08,163
they'll go, "What's this oven?"

624
00:23:08,823 --> 00:23:10,392
- He's strategic. - The smell of butter, right?

625
00:23:10,393 --> 00:23:12,663
- The smell of butter is the best. - That's right.

626
00:23:13,163 --> 00:23:14,633
(His mouth is watering already.)

627
00:23:16,133 --> 00:23:18,702
(Moomoo's savory strategy...)

628
00:23:18,703 --> 00:23:21,243
(gets toasted in a golden color.)

629
00:23:21,973 --> 00:23:23,973
Do you want to buy snacks?

630
00:23:24,673 --> 00:23:27,013
Yes, we should buy some beverages and snacks.

631
00:23:27,283 --> 00:23:29,313
- Luxurious-looking snacks. - Yes.

632
00:23:29,683 --> 00:23:30,853
High-end snacks.

633
00:23:31,483 --> 00:23:33,682
- Thank you. - Thank you. Have a nice day.

634
00:23:33,683 --> 00:23:36,123
(For breakfast, they choose hearty gukbap instead of gimbap.)

635
00:23:36,783 --> 00:23:39,192
(They go back to the studio...)

636
00:23:39,193 --> 00:23:41,363
(with breakfast to go.)

637
00:23:44,793 --> 00:23:46,033
He set something up.

638
00:23:47,163 --> 00:23:48,332
What's this?

639
00:23:48,333 --> 00:23:49,503
(Staring)

640
00:23:50,803 --> 00:23:54,242
You guys look like the young owners who have just opened a cafe.

641
00:23:54,243 --> 00:23:55,943
- The fearless ones. - Yes.

642
00:23:58,173 --> 00:23:59,373
- All right. - Hyun Moo.

643
00:23:59,713 --> 00:24:00,743
Hey.

644
00:24:01,213 --> 00:24:02,483
We bought gukbap.

645
00:24:03,383 --> 00:24:05,312
- Gukbap sounds good. - We bought bean sprout gukbap.

646
00:24:05,313 --> 00:24:06,982
Good. We only have ten minutes left.

647
00:24:06,983 --> 00:24:08,623
We can finish gukbap in five minutes.

648
00:24:08,723 --> 00:24:09,723
Okay.

649
00:24:11,393 --> 00:24:12,623
I love that dish.

650
00:24:13,323 --> 00:24:14,723
I'll eat that at home.

651
00:24:16,663 --> 00:24:18,903
(Since there isn't much time, he hurriedly takes a sip.)

652
00:24:21,033 --> 00:24:22,162
It's tasty.

653
00:24:22,163 --> 00:24:23,933
Hyun Moo, it won't be right...

654
00:24:24,333 --> 00:24:27,872
to bring down the price too much.

655
00:24:27,873 --> 00:24:28,942
That's right.

656
00:24:28,943 --> 00:24:30,703
- The profits go to a good cause. - Exactly.

657
00:24:30,873 --> 00:24:33,033
If the price is too low, the buyers will feel bad too.

658
00:24:33,983 --> 00:24:35,342
But sell your clothes at a low price.

659
00:24:35,343 --> 00:24:36,942
(CODE KUNST, sell your clothes at a low price.)

660
00:24:36,943 --> 00:24:38,652
- You know, - His clothes are amazing.

661
00:24:38,653 --> 00:24:40,623
There's a crazy look in his eyes.

662
00:24:40,923 --> 00:24:41,923
But sell your clothes at a low price.

663
00:24:41,924 --> 00:24:42,952
His eyes...

664
00:24:42,953 --> 00:24:44,799
My eyes go crazy when I see CODE KUNST's clothes.

665
00:24:44,823 --> 00:24:47,262
I still can't forget the craziness he has shown...

666
00:24:47,263 --> 00:24:49,343
when he came upstairs at my place in Seorae Village.

667
00:24:49,763 --> 00:24:50,932
It's a Gen Z brand.

668
00:24:50,933 --> 00:24:54,463
(He bought all CODE KUNST's clothes in Seorae Village.)

669
00:24:55,433 --> 00:24:58,173
(Not even CODE KUNST could stop Hyun Moo's craziness.)

670
00:24:58,603 --> 00:25:00,103
The white top I got from him...

671
00:25:00,203 --> 00:25:02,202
turned yellow because I wore it too much.

672
00:25:02,203 --> 00:25:04,042
- I wear all of his clothes. - Hyun Moo wears them often.

673
00:25:04,043 --> 00:25:05,043
I wear them often.

674
00:25:05,044 --> 00:25:06,472
Seeing him wear them often makes me feel proud.

675
00:25:06,473 --> 00:25:07,989
I wear them until they become tattered.

676
00:25:08,013 --> 00:25:10,012
We need a client like you.

677
00:25:10,013 --> 00:25:11,013
- Exactly. - That's right.

678
00:25:11,014 --> 00:25:13,153
- Clients who want to spend money. - That's right.

679
00:25:13,853 --> 00:25:16,583
I told my friend to bring 2,000 dollars in cash.

680
00:25:17,823 --> 00:25:19,393
Your friend? Who?

681
00:25:20,093 --> 00:25:21,263
He'll come later.

682
00:25:21,523 --> 00:25:22,693
- Will he come later? - Yes.

683
00:25:24,463 --> 00:25:26,833
(He adds rice to his soup.)

684
00:25:28,033 --> 00:25:29,809
I can't believe CODE KUNST added rice to the soup.

685
00:25:29,833 --> 00:25:31,832
We turned you into a proper person.

686
00:25:31,833 --> 00:25:33,833
Now, I can't do anything without eating breakfast.

687
00:25:34,103 --> 00:25:35,173
It's a nice change.

688
00:25:35,873 --> 00:25:37,772
(Slurping)

689
00:25:37,773 --> 00:25:38,872
Now...

690
00:25:38,873 --> 00:25:41,143
Why are you eating like a lunatic?

691
00:25:41,613 --> 00:25:45,012
(Feeding on bean sprouts)

692
00:25:45,013 --> 00:25:46,983
- He's eating all the bean sprouts. - Now...

693
00:25:47,553 --> 00:25:49,522
Why are you eating like a lunatic?

694
00:25:49,523 --> 00:25:50,852
- He's eating all the bean sprouts. - Hey.

695
00:25:50,853 --> 00:25:52,052
He's gnawing on them.

696
00:25:52,053 --> 00:25:53,522
Are the bean sprouts coming out or going in?

697
00:25:53,523 --> 00:25:54,792
- The bean sprouts... - You know,

698
00:25:54,793 --> 00:25:56,822
- the bean sprouts look aggressive. - Yes.

699
00:25:56,823 --> 00:25:59,033
No, Kian84 is eating them aggressively.

700
00:25:59,163 --> 00:26:00,492
It's like a comic book from Ito Junji.

701
00:26:00,493 --> 00:26:03,103
I was happy that there were a lot of bean sprouts.

702
00:26:03,763 --> 00:26:04,773
(Grunting)

703
00:26:07,133 --> 00:26:08,273
My goodness.

704
00:26:08,843 --> 00:26:10,003
I feel much better now.

705
00:26:11,513 --> 00:26:12,843
We don't have much time now.

706
00:26:14,313 --> 00:26:16,042
(They hurriedly finish setting up the 1st floor.)

707
00:26:16,043 --> 00:26:17,213
Attention, everyone.

708
00:26:17,653 --> 00:26:19,283
(That came out of nowhere.)

709
00:26:19,953 --> 00:26:21,883
- Did you draw again? - It isn't like that.

710
00:26:22,253 --> 00:26:25,423
Every hip boutique has the name in writing.

711
00:26:26,353 --> 00:26:27,863
Would you bring the easel?

712
00:26:28,123 --> 00:26:30,162
The clients should become excited upon entering.

713
00:26:30,163 --> 00:26:31,863
Do you need an easel this big?

714
00:26:35,363 --> 00:26:37,932
(Grand Rainbow Bazaar will shine...)

715
00:26:37,933 --> 00:26:39,202
(with Moosquiat's new work.)

716
00:26:39,203 --> 00:26:40,772
Isn't it pretty?

717
00:26:40,773 --> 00:26:41,873
It's cute.

718
00:26:42,403 --> 00:26:44,342
- It's cute. - Isn't it cute?

719
00:26:44,343 --> 00:26:46,073
It looks a bit treacherous.

720
00:26:46,343 --> 00:26:48,343
I think I've seen it in a loan company commercial.

721
00:26:49,013 --> 00:26:50,752
- Moomoo Market. - Okay.

722
00:26:50,753 --> 00:26:51,783
Isn't it cute?

723
00:26:52,383 --> 00:26:53,582
- It's so annoying... - It's nice.

724
00:26:53,583 --> 00:26:55,683
That he wrote "Market" in cursive.

725
00:26:56,823 --> 00:26:58,153
Isn't it very old-fashioned?

726
00:26:58,993 --> 00:27:00,593
Still, the color combination is pretty.

727
00:27:00,863 --> 00:27:02,062
He's good at painting.

728
00:27:02,063 --> 00:27:03,192
They're so nice to Hyun Moo.

729
00:27:03,193 --> 00:27:04,332
Hyun Moo is good at picking the right colors.

730
00:27:04,333 --> 00:27:06,932
Seriously, it wouldn't have been pretty without the red writing.

731
00:27:06,933 --> 00:27:08,103
That's right.

732
00:27:08,403 --> 00:27:10,402
- It's cute. - If I can't sell anything,

733
00:27:10,403 --> 00:27:13,003
I'll sell the painting at a cheap price.

734
00:27:14,603 --> 00:27:16,802
- I want to buy it. - "Market" is in cursive.

735
00:27:16,803 --> 00:27:18,472
- Really? Do you want to buy it? - Yes. I'm drawn to it.

736
00:27:18,473 --> 00:27:19,872
- The painting? - Yes, I'm drawn to it.

737
00:27:19,873 --> 00:27:21,112
- Really? - Really?

738
00:27:21,113 --> 00:27:22,682
- It's for a good cause. - That's right.

739
00:27:22,683 --> 00:27:24,259
- Give me 50 dollars then. - I'll buy it for 50 dollars.

740
00:27:24,283 --> 00:27:25,952
- Is 50 dollars a good price? - Okay.

741
00:27:25,953 --> 00:27:27,453
I'll take it for 100 dollars.

742
00:27:27,823 --> 00:27:28,952
- I really want to buy it. - Hyun Moo.

743
00:27:28,953 --> 00:27:30,352
You sold your painting.

744
00:27:30,353 --> 00:27:32,692
- Seriously. It's the first time. - He said the red was a nice accent.

745
00:27:32,693 --> 00:27:35,262
CODE KUNST is good at business.

746
00:27:35,263 --> 00:27:36,592
I didn't like it at first, but the red writing...

747
00:27:36,593 --> 00:27:38,532
- drew me in. - It's an accent.

748
00:27:38,533 --> 00:27:39,762
- One hundred dollars. - Spend some more.

749
00:27:39,763 --> 00:27:41,762
- After all... - I'll give you 300 dollars.

750
00:27:41,763 --> 00:27:42,933
Just spend 500 dollars.

751
00:27:43,733 --> 00:27:45,472
- After all, it's for a good cause. - It's for a good cause.

752
00:27:45,473 --> 00:27:47,079
- It's for a good cause. - It's all for a good cause.

753
00:27:47,103 --> 00:27:48,672
- It suits your place. - I'll put it on the rooftop.

754
00:27:48,673 --> 00:27:50,602
- It'll be nice. - Okay. I'll give you 500 dollars.

755
00:27:50,603 --> 00:27:51,672
- Five hundred dollars? Really? - Five hundred dollars.

756
00:27:51,673 --> 00:27:53,042
- It's for a good cause. - That's right.

757
00:27:53,043 --> 00:27:56,282
It's my first time buying a painting.

758
00:27:56,283 --> 00:27:57,852
I can't believe I'm buying your painting for 500 dollars.

759
00:27:57,853 --> 00:27:59,489
- You have an eye for the arts. - You know,

760
00:27:59,513 --> 00:28:00,982
- the first transaction matters. - That's right.

761
00:28:00,983 --> 00:28:02,022
It's for a good cause.

762
00:28:02,023 --> 00:28:03,852
It'll be better if you put your autograph on it.

763
00:28:03,853 --> 00:28:05,892
- The value will go up. - I'll do that.

764
00:28:05,893 --> 00:28:07,362
I'll write a journal as well.

765
00:28:07,363 --> 00:28:09,092
